  abstract = {We develop the holographic dictionary for pure \$\textbackslash mathrm\{AdS\}\_3\$ gravity where the Lagrangian of the dual \$2d\$ conformal field theory has been deformed by an arbitrary function of the energy-momentum tensor. In addition to the \$T \textbackslash overline\{T\}\$ deformation, examples of such functions include a class of marginal stress tensor deformations which are special because they leave the generating functional of connected correlators unchanged up to a redefinition of the source and expectation value. Within this marginal class, we identify the unique deformation that commutes with the \$T \textbackslash overline\{T\}\$ flow, which is the root-\$T \textbackslash overline\{T\}\$ operator, and write down the modified boundary conditions corresponding to this root-\$T \textbackslash overline\{T\}\$ deformation. We also identify the unique marginal stress tensor flow for the cylinder spectrum of the dual CFT which commutes with the inviscid Burgers' flow driven by \$T \textbackslash overline\{T\}\$, and we propose this unique flow as a candidate root-\$T \textbackslash overline\{T\}\$ deformation of the energy levels. We study BTZ black holes in \$\textbackslash mathrm\{AdS\}\_3\$ subject to root-\$T \textbackslash overline\{T\}\$ deformed boundary conditions, and find that their masses flow in a way which is identical to that of our candidate root-\$T \textbackslash overline\{T\}\$ energy flow equation, which offers evidence that this flow is the correct one. Finally, we also obtain the root-\$T \textbackslash overline\{T\}\$ deformed boundary conditions for the gauge field in the Chern-Simons formulation of \$\textbackslash mathrm\{AdS\}\_3\$ gravity.},
